    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0282" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.60d Finnish Vessels/150.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Finnish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Järnefelt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-01">February 1, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Excellency that on January 30, 1935, a complete record in two volumes,<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d159-f1"/> regarding the claims for the detention of 13
                    Finnish sailing vessels for various periods during 1918, prepared by Mr. John G.
                    Poore, Attorney at Law, has been handed to the Legal Adviser of the Department
                    of State, Mr. Hackworth.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eero Järnefelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
